1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,200
Why does the writer not understand the porter?
为什么作者听不懂搬运工的话？

2
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:20,730
Why does the writer not understand the porter?
为什么作者听不懂搬运工的话？

3
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:25,820
I arrived in London at last.
我终于到了伦敦。

4
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:31,580
The railway station was big, black and dark.
火车站很大，又黑又暗。

5
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:38,030
I did not know the way to my hotel, so I asked a porter.
我不知道去旅馆的路，于是向一个搬运工打听。

6
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:46,240
I not only spoke English very carefully, but very clearly as well.
我的英语讲得不仅非常认真，而且咬字也非常清楚。

7
00:00:47,410 --> 00:00:50,960
The porter, however, could not understand me.
然而搬运工却不明白我的话。

8
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:58,460
I repeated my question several times and at last he understood.
我把问话重复了好几遍，他终于听懂了。

9
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:05,640
he answered me, but he spoke neither slowly nor clearly.
他回答了，但他讲得既不慢也不清楚。

10
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:10,550
'I am a foreigner,' I said.
“我是个外国人，”我说。

11
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:13,620
Then he spoke slowly,
于是他说得慢了，

12
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:17,150
but I could not understand him.
可我还是听不懂。

13
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:20,830
My teacher never spoke English like that!
我的老师从来不那样讲英语！

14
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:26,570
The porter and I looked at each other and smiled.
搬运工和我相视一笑。

15
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:31,090
Then he said something and I understood it.
接着他说了点什么，这回我听懂了。

16
00:01:33,130 --> 00:01:36,660
'You'll soon learn English!' he said.
“您会很快学会英语的！”他说。

17
00:01:37,770 --> 00:01:38,880
I wonder.
我感到奇怪。

18
00:01:39,710 --> 00:01:43,780
In England, each person speaks a different language.
在英国，人们讲着各自不同的语言。

19
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:49,250
The English understand each other, but I don't understand them!
英国人之间相互听得懂，可我却听不懂他们的话！

20
00:01:49,930 --> 00:01:51,980
Do they speak English?
他们讲的是英语吗？
